I haven't seen this one mentioned, either in the spoilers file or in the
group; maybe only my roommate, who came up with it, is twisted enough to
try stunts like this.

I personally do *NOT* do this -- it's cheating on a plane beyond keeping
backups of your save files.  I don't think there's a reasonable way for it
to be eliminated from the game, either, though I may be wrong.  I'm posting
just to let the world know that it exists.

Okay, if you don't want to be tempted, hit n now.

Are you sure?  This is an ugly one!

Okay, fine, you asked for it.

This definitely works on PCs, and will probably work under UNIX if the
permissions are right, and you know where the levels files are kept.

Step 1: Stand next to stairs up on level X.
Step 2: Drop all your stuff.
Step 3: Walk upstairs.
Step 4: Shell to the OS.
Step 5: Copy levels.X to levels.bak.  Return to the game.
Step 6: Go back downstairs, pick up all your stuff, and walk upstairs
again.
Step 7: Shell out, and copy levels.bak to levels.X.
Step 8: Back to the game.  Walk downstairs and... pick up your stuff again!

That's right, you can clone stuff -- any stuff -- ad nauseam.

Haven't tried it with named weapons and such -- in fact, I don't try it at
all.  Out-and-out cheating.  Use at your own risk.  Your mileage may vary.

